---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import CallButton from '../components/CallButton.astro';
import CallPanel from '../components/CallPanel.astro';
import ServiceGrid from '../components/ServiceGrid.astro';
import CityGrid from '../components/CityGrid.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { SITE, RENTER, isRented } from '../config/site.js';
import { GENERAL_FAQS } from '../data/faqs.js';
import { faqSchema } from '../lib/schema.js';
const faqs = GENERAL_FAQS.slice(0, 5);
const rented = isRented();
---
<Base
  title={`${SITE.name} | Roof Replacement & Repair in Lake Oswego, West Linn & Oregon City`}
  description="Roof leaking, mossy or just old? Straight answers on roof costs, permits and materials for Portland's south metro, and one call to talk with a CCB-licensed local roofer."
  schema={[faqSchema(faqs)]}
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding:0" data-hero>
    <div class="hero-media"><Photo slot="hero" eager sizes="100vw" widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1920, 2400]} /></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="copy">
        <h1>A dry, solid roof over your family, without the guesswork.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Oregon winters find every weak spot. Call to talk with a {rented ? 'licensed' : 'local, CCB-licensed'} roofer about what your roof needs and what it should cost.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <CallButton label="Call" size="lg" />
          <a class="btn btn-on-dark btn-lg" href="/roof-cost-estimator/">Estimate my cost</a>
        </div>
        <p class="note">{rented ? `${RENTER.businessName}, Oregon CCB #${RENTER.ccbNumber}.` : 'Free to call. If we miss you, leave a message and we\'ll get back to you.'}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>You shouldn't have to become a roofing expert to protect your home.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Maybe there's a new stain on the ceiling after the last storm. Maybe the moss is winning, or the roof is pushing 25 and you can't tell if it has one winter left or five. Then come quotes thousands apart, door-knockers after every windstorm, and the worry of getting a $15,000+ decision wrong.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problems">
        <article class="problem big">
          <figure><Photo slot="rain-roof" sizes="(min-width:900px) 55vw, 100vw" /></figure>
          <h3>The leak you can't pin down</h3>
          <p>Water travels. The stain is rarely where the hole is, and every rainy week it spreads into insulation and drywall.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="problem small">
          <figure><Photo slot="moss" sizes="(min-width:900px) 200px, 100vw" /></figure>
          <div>
            <h3>Moss, needles and clogged gutters</h3>
            <p>Shade and eight wet months make south metro roofs prime moss habitat, and moss holds water against the shingles.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="problem small">
          <figure><Photo slot="inspection" sizes="(min-width:900px) 200px, 100vw" /></figure>
          <div>
            <h3>Who do you trust?</h3>
            <p>Bids that don't match, vague warranties, contractors you can't check. It's hard to know what a fair price looks like.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>{rented ? `${RENTER.businessName}: local roofers who explain before they quote.` : 'One call to a licensed local roofer. That\'s the whole plan.'}</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--on-dark-2)">{rented
          ? 'We know these neighborhoods, the permit offices and the weather. You get a clear inspection, a written bid, and a roof built for Oregon rain.'
          : `${SITE.name} is a local resource, not a contractor. We've done the homework on costs, permits and materials for the south metro, and we connect callers with an independent roofer who holds an active Oregon CCB license.`}</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Call and describe the roof</h3><p>Your city, what's going on, and when you'd like help. If we miss you, leave a message and we'll get back to you.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Get a look from a licensed roofer</h3><p>You get their business name and Oregon CCB # before anyone climbs a ladder, so you can check it yourself.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Decide with a written bid</h3><p>Materials, warranty, permit and price in writing. No pressure and no obligation.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:var(--s5)">
        <CallButton label="Call" size="lg" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Whatever your roof needs</h2>
        <p class="lead">From one leaky vent boot to a full tear-off: what each job involves and what it typically costs here.</p>
      </div>
      <ServiceGrid />
      <p style="margin-top:var(--s3)"><a class="text-link" href="/roofing-materials/">Compare roofing materials: asphalt, metal, cedar shake and flat roofs</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-fog">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stakes">
        <div class="bad">
          <h3>Wait another winter, and</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A small leak rots decking and soaks insulation</li>
            <li>Ceiling, drywall and paint repairs pile onto the roof bill</li>
            <li>Moss damage that insurance usually won't cover</li>
            <li>A rushed decision after a storm, with whoever's free</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="good">
          <h3>Get ahead of it, and</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A dry house through the whole rainy season</li>
            <li>A fair price you understand, in writing</li>
            <li>A licensed roofer you checked yourself</li>
            <li>One less thing to worry about for decades</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="tools">
        <div class="tool-feature">
          <Photo slot="shingles" sizes="(min-width:900px) 55vw, 100vw" />
          <h2>Know your numbers before anyone climbs a ladder</h2>
          <p class="measure">The estimator turns your home's size and roof pitch into a price range from published Oregon and Portland-area cost data, with every source listed. No sign-up; the range shows right away.</p>
          <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/roof-cost-estimator/">Open the cost estimator</a></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="tool-list">
          <li>
            <h3>Oregon Homeowner's Roof Replacement Guide</h3>
            <p>Eight printable pages: signs it's time, materials for our climate, vetting a CCB-licensed roofer, reading a bid, permits, insurance and moss care. Direct download, no email.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/downloads/oregon-roof-replacement-guide.pdf" download>Download the PDF</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Roof leaking right now?</h3>
            <p>The storm and leak first-steps checklist: safety, containing water, photos for insurance, and tarping.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/resources/storm-leak-checklist/">Open the checklist</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>What a new roof costs here</h3>
            <p>Sourced ranges for Lake Oswego, West Linn, Oregon City, Gladstone and Milwaukie.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/roof-replacement-cost/">Read the cost guide</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-fog">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Local to Portland's south metro</h2>
        <p class="lead">Each city has its own housing stock, permit office and tree rules. Start with yours.</p>
      </div>
      <CityGrid />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap layout-2">
      <div>
        <h2>Roofing questions we hear most</h2>
        {faqs.map((f) => <details><summary>{f.q}</summary><div class="a" set:html={f.a} /></details>)}
        <p style="margin-top:var(--s3)"><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">See all questions</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="sticky-side"><CallPanel /></aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
